  "notes": "The atmosphere-forward end of modern Memphis: \"eerie beats … tons of atmosphere\" under a slouched drawl. Two parameters carry it and both are unusual for the lane. (1) **The sub is not the only low voice.** The research documents a separately played bass on several tracks alongside the tuned 808, so `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.6, a register reaching 46 and three passing tones — a bass that moves under the pads rather than mirroring the kick. (2) The instrument set is guitar, bass, mellotron, strings and piano, which the research calls unusually wide for the lane, so the harmony is real slow-moving pad motion — i–VI and i–VII families over 4-bar loops, `voicing.style` open across 44–76, sevenths at 0.26 — and the melody is a long-sustain, low-density bed (1–3 notes a bar, 4- and 8-bar phrases, `emptyBarBias` 0.3). The kit is deliberately quiet against that: the lowest velocity tiers here, percs at −6 dB, and `pitchWalk` 3 with `gapProb` 0.62 for the restrained, gappy roll the mix asks for. ⚠ `medium`, per the research: the vocal characterisation, the atmosphere and instrumentation, and the chart facts are sourced, **and the tempo band 128–152 straight is the inferred parameter**. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 43 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 44 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3. ⚠ **The countermelody reached only 941 distinct answers in 1000 seeds against a floor of 980**, so it was given range: densityRatio 0.45. A counter is combinatorial in the styles it may pick, its density against the melody, and the phrase length it answers inside — one style over a thin density inside a single phrase length has almost nothing a seed can vary. ⚠ **The countermelody reached 943/1000 distinct answers against a floor of 980**, so its style pool was opened: answer_lick, bell_echo, densityRatio 0.55. ⛔ `counter.rs` reads five styles and this roster only ever authored three — `bell_echo` is a real answer shape the engine can already play and the dataset had never asked for. ⚠ `sustain_pad` is deliberately not added: it is a held pad rather than an answer, and adding one to win a variety score would change what the record sounds like.",
